One source compiled into two libraries (a native copy and a Melange copy,
like `ahkit/native` and `ahkit/src`) has the same module name, scope,
binding and content, so it gets the same class and the same variable
names. `generate` over both copies passes the collision check and writes
each block once.

  $ cat > dune-project << EOF
  > (lang dune 3.10)
  > (using melange 0.1)
  > EOF

  $ mkdir native src

  $ cat > native/dune << EOF
  > (copy_files ../shared/*.re)
  > (library
  >  (name ahkit_native)
  >  (wrapped false)
  >  (libraries styled-ppx.native)
  >  (preprocess
  >   (pps styled-ppx --native)))
  > EOF

  $ cat > src/dune << EOF
  > (copy_files ../shared/*.re)
  > (library
  >  (name ahkit)
  >  (wrapped false)
  >  (modes melange)
  >  (libraries styled-ppx.melange)
  >  (preprocess
  >   (pps styled-ppx melange.ppx)))
  > EOF

  $ dune build

  $ styled-ppx.generate _build/default/native/Button.re.pp.ml > native.css
  $ styled-ppx.generate _build/default/src/.melange_src/Button.re.pp.ml > src.css
  $ diff native.css src.css
  $ styled-ppx.generate _build/default/native/Button.re.pp.ml _build/default/src/.melange_src/Button.re.pp.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  @property --10pjmpy-0{syntax:"*";inherits:false;}
  .css-10pjmpy{color:var(--10pjmpy-0);}.css-10pjmpy:hover{border-color:var(--10pjmpy-0);}
  .css-thc0ay{padding:4px;}
